{{Quote|My favorite podracer is from Troiken. You ever watched Gasgano? He's the greatest!|[[Sprocket]]|<ref name="Hunters">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref>}}
'''Gasgano''' was a [[Xexto]] [[Gender|male]] [[podracer]] [[pilot]] who participated in the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]] on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]]. Gasgano wanted nothing more than to win the race, piloting his [[Color|green]] ''[[Ord Pedrovia]]'' podracer. For the majority of the race, Gasgano tailed the leaders, but ended up losing to the [[human]] [[Anakin Skywalker]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|&hellip;eh Gasgano doowa newpa Ord Petrovia!|[[Fodesinbeed Annodue]] introduces Gasgano during the Boonta Eve Classic|<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref>}}
A [[Xexto]] [[Gender|male]], Gasgano performed as a professional [[podracer]] [[pilot]], flying a [[Color|green]] ''[[Ord Pedrovia]]'' podracer. Gasgano raced for high-speed thrills, and his four spindly arms made him perfectly suited for racing, able to use all of his arms at once to pilot his pod. Extremely competitive, he disliked the prospect of losing, and joined the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]], racing for [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder|Gardulla]] the [[Hutt]]<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> on the [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]], which took place ten [[Standard year|years]] prior to the [[The galaxy|intergalactic]] [[Clone Wars]], in order to beat the local champion, the [[Dug]] [[Sebulba]].<ref name="DB" /> Gasgano's competition also included two-time Boonta winner [[Boles Roor]], returning Boonta competitor [[Dud Bolt]], and the [[Er'Kit (species)|Er'Kit]] [[Ody Mandrell]], who employed a team of record setting [[DUM-series pit droid|pit droids]].<ref name="TPM" /> Gasgano also had it in his mind to beat the [[human]] competitor [[Anakin Skywalker]].<ref name="DB" /> The Boonta was held at the [[Mos Espa Grand Arena]], and the ''Ord Pedrovia'' was placed in the middle of the third role, next to Roor's podracer, and directly behind Bolt's and Skywalker's racers.<ref name="TPM" />

The [[Troig]] race announcer [[Fodesinbeed Annodue|Beed]], speaking in [[Huttese]], introduced Gasgano and his podracer shortly before the race's host, [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the Hutt, announced the official start of the race. The podracers darted off with the exception of two: Skywalker and [[Ben Quadinaros]], both having stalled. It wasn't long before Gasgano was behind the leaders, having overtaken Mandrell, Roor, Bolt, and several other racers. Eventually, Skywalker repaired his podracer and entered the course, and overtook the pilots behind Gasgano. The crafty Xexto attempted to block Skywalker's attempts at passing, but was bested when the Human flew over the ''Ord Pedrovia'' following a cliff drop. Gasgano attempted to retake lost ground, and briefly overtook Skywalker after the Human lost a scuffle to Sebulba. However, the lead over Skywalker didn't last long, and Gasgano was trapped behind the two leaders. During the final stretch of the third lap, Sebulba crashed after a second tangle with Skywalker, allowing Gasgano to gain ground and beat at least one more competitor, albeit his last. Ultimately, Skywalker won the Boonta<ref name="TPM" /> and Gasgano finished in second place.<ref name="Ultimate SW" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:GasganoPodracer-NTIP.png|thumb|right|300px|Gasgano's Ord Pedrovia podracer]]
Gasgano's four arms granted him an amount of dexterity that pilots with fewer limbs could not achieve. With greater control over his podracer, Gasgano's biology was uniquely suited for podracing. Gasgano was also very competitive and did what he could to make sure other pilots would not pass him. A Xexto, he stood 1.22 [[meter]]s tall, and exhibited brown and white skin, with some splotches of purple around his face. His large [[eye]]s were solidly black.<ref name="DB" />

==Equipment==
Gasgano piloted an ''Ord Pedrovia'' podracer that was green in color. The [[cockpit]] had a [[camera]] installed on the back of it, which fed to a [[Viewscreen|holoscreen]] on the dash. This device allowed Gasgano to monitor activity behind him. He used it to great effect throughout the race, including a moment where he was able to block all of Skywalker's attempts to pass. When racing, Gasgano wore [[goggles]] to protect his eyes.<ref name="TPM" />

==Behind the scenes==
Gasgano was created for the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']],<ref name="TPM" /> but first appeared in the film's [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace (novelization)|novelization]], written by [[Terry Brooks]]. In the novel, Gasgano not only participated in the Boonta, but in a race that took place before it as well.<ref name="Novel">[[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace (novelization)|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'' novelization]]</ref> Detailed concept art of Gasgano was illustrated by [[Terryl Whitlatch]], [[Jay Shuster]], and [[Iain McCaig]], while a detailed sculpture was created by the film's art department.<ref name="ISG">[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''Insider's Guide'']]</ref> In the film, Gasgano was rendered wholly with CGI.<ref name="DB2">{{DB|character|gasgano|Gasgano}}</ref>

